<h2>The pricing question</h2>

<p>Pricing is where the difference becomes most obvious. A small business owner who needs CRM, email marketing, a funnel builder, SMS, automation, and review management would need to combine multiple HubSpot Hubs at professional-tier pricing. That adds up to well over $1,000 USD per month before factoring in add-ons and contact limits.</p>

<p>DUSA includes all of those features in a single plan that costs a fraction of that. For a sole operator or small team, the maths is not close.</p>

<p>It is also worth noting that HubSpot charges based on contacts. As your database grows, so does your bill. DUSA does not penalise you for growing your contact list. Your pricing stays the same whether you have 100 contacts or 10,000.</p>

<h2>The complexity question</h2>

<p>HubSpot is designed for teams that have the time and expertise to configure complex systems. There is an entire ecosystem of HubSpot consultants and agencies that exist specifically because the platform is difficult to set up and optimise without help. That is not a criticism. It reflects the reality that HubSpot is built for a different audience.</p>

<p>DUSA is built for the business owner who is also the marketing department, the sales team, and the customer service rep. If you do not have the luxury of spending weeks configuring your software, DUSA gets you operational faster with less overhead.</p>

<h2>When HubSpot is the better choice</h2>

<p>HubSpot is the better choice if you have a marketing team of five or more people, a budget of $1,000+ per month for software, and complex enterprise needs like custom reporting dashboards, multi-touch attribution modelling, or deep integrations with enterprise software. If you are a growing company with 50+ employees and need a platform that scales to enterprise level, HubSpot was built for that.</p>

<h2>When DUSA is the better choice</h2>

<p>DUSA is the better choice if you are a sole operator or small team, you want everything in one place without piecing together multiple Hubs, you need to be up and running quickly, and your budget does not stretch to $1,000+ per month in software costs. If you value simplicity and integration over depth you will never use, DUSA is built for your reality. For a deeper look at why consolidation wins, see our <a href="/blog/all-in-one-vs-separate-tools">all-in-one vs separate tools comparison</a>.</p>

<blockquote><p>The best platform is not the one with the most features. It is the one you will actually use, every day, without needing a consultant to help you.</p></blockquote>

<div class="divider">...</div>

<h2>The bottom line</h2>

<p>HubSpot and DUSA solve the same core problem. They help you manage contacts, market your business, automate your follow-ups, and grow your revenue. The difference is in who they are built for.</p>

<p>HubSpot is a powerful enterprise platform that can do almost anything, if you have the budget and the team to unlock it. DUSA is a focused platform that gives small business owners everything they need without the complexity or cost they do not.</p>

<p>Neither is objectively "better." But for the sole operator or small team trying to grow without drowning in software, DUSA is the more practical choice.</p>

